	"identifying_description": "edition of 30",
	"web_text": "Conceived by Erick Lyle and Marshall Weber, STREETOPIA is an assemblage of works by twenty-four current and former San Francisco artists associated with the art movements known as the Mission School and the New Mission School. Lyle traces the project's origins to a cement graffiti tag reading \"Glitter Doll\" that he encountered on Twenty-First Street near Capp Street in the Mission. He was soon imagining the stories behind other scratches and drawings that appear all over this ever-changing city. Each book in the variable edition of 30 is subtitled with the name of a different San Francisco neighborhood and features unique works of art.",
	"didactic_label": "Conceived by Erick Lyle and Marshall Weber, STREETOPIA is an assemblage of works by twenty-four current and former San Francisco artists associated with the art movements known as the Mission School and the New Mission School. Lyle traces the project's origins to a cement graffiti tag reading “Glitter Doll” that he encountered on Twenty-First Street near Capp Street in the Mission. He was soon imagining the stories behind other scratches and drawings that appear all over this ever-changing city. Each book in the variable edition of 30 is subtitled with the name of a different San Francisco neighborhood and features unique works of art.",
	"exhibition_history_text": "California BookWorks\nCPLH, Logan Gallery, May 7 to October 16, 2016",
